From 6e2a67d343cac504606c74e4144f1f88f6f0f562 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Tom F." <tomf@tomtomtech.net>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:55:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(a2a): upgrade a2a-protocol-types to 0.12

The `a2a-v1` feature has pinned 0.5 since the integration landed in #273;
upstream is at 0.12.0. Three breaking changes affect this crate, all from
0.7.0; 0.8.0 through 0.12.0 are additive for the types used here.

- `JsonRpcRequest.id` is now the `JsonRpcRequestId` enum, which separates an
  absent id (a JSON-RPC notification) from an explicit null (a call). All
  twelve sites in `jsonrpc_handler.rs` build a *response* id, so each uses
  the `to_response_id()` method added upstream for that purpose.

- `AuthenticationInfo.credentials` is now `Option<String>`. The push sender
  omits the `Authorization` header when no credential is present rather than
  sending an empty `Bearer `.

- `TaskPushNotificationConfig.task_id` is now `Option<String>`. The REST
  binding assigns it from the path. The JSON-RPC binding has no path, so a
  standalone `CreateTaskPushNotificationConfig` whose body omits `taskId` is
  rejected with -32602 INVALID_PARAMS; without that guard the handler looks
  up the empty task id and answers -32001 TASK_NOT_FOUND.

Two user-visible corrections follow, both recorded in CHANGELOG.md: the
agent card no longer emits the v0.3 top-level `url` that the A2A v1.0 JSON
schema rejects, and the push-config error above.

No example source changes were needed. The two example manifests that pin
the crate directly move to 0.12 and resolve to one version, since both take
adk-server by path.

Signed-off-by: Tom F. <tomf@tomtomtech.net>
Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
