diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index eb8ffe7c..a398480c 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -23,6 +23,22 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
   use `with_reasoning_replay_field(ReasoningReplayField::Reasoning)` to send
   `reasoning`. Replay emits only the selected field; standard OpenAI and
   Azure requests omit both fields by default.
+
+- **Spec-compliant agent card** (`adk-server`, `a2a-v1`): the card served at
+  `/.well-known/agent.json` no longer emits the v0.3 top-level `url`, which the
+  A2A v1.0 JSON schema rejects (`'url' does not match any of the regexes`).
+  `supportedInterfaces` already carries the address. This follows from the
+  `a2a-protocol-types` 0.5 -> 0.12 upgrade, which stopped serializing the field
+  while still parsing it, so cards published by v0.3 peers still load.
+
+- **Correct error for a push config with no task ID** (`adk-server`, `a2a-v1`):
+  `CreateTaskPushNotificationConfig` over JSON-RPC now returns `-32602`
+  `INVALID_PARAMS` when the config body omits `taskId`, instead of looking up the
+  empty task id and reporting `-32001` `TASK_NOT_FOUND` with the message
+  `Task not found: `. `taskId` became optional on the wire type in
+  `a2a-protocol-types` 0.7.0 because a config nested in `SendMessageConfiguration`
+  legitimately omits it; a standalone create still requires one, and the REST
+  binding supplies it from the path.
 - **Open Responses argument identity** (`adk-model`): conflicting item or call
   identities terminate compatible streams before cached arguments can cross
   tool calls. Blank completed snapshots restore matching streamed arguments
